\chapter{Building, installing, and validating MuDSL}
The C++ toolkit requires C++20. The D module depends on Phobos. Standard
builds do not require the separate legacy MetaML sources. The top-level CMake
project exports an interface target named \api{MuDSL::MuDSL}.

\begin{code}
cmake -S . -B build -DBUILD_EXAMPLES=ON
cmake --build build -j4
ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure
cmake --install build --prefix /your/prefix
\end{code}

When an LDC, DMD, or GDC compiler is available, the tests also build and run
the D toolkit and MuLL embedding. Set \api{MuDSL_TEST_D=OFF} to omit those
targets. Lua preprocessing tests are opt-in through \api{MuDSL_TEST_LUA}.

\section{Consume an installed package}
\begin{code}
find_package(MuDSL CONFIG REQUIRED)
target_link_libraries(my_application PRIVATE MuDSL::MuDSL)
\end{code}
The header and D module are installed in the include directory. Native MuLL
sources are installed under \api{include/mull/stdlib}, and package files are
also available under \api{share/mull/stdlib}. Pass the latter path to the
runtime when running an installed application. Package discovery is explicit;
it does not infer the installation prefix from an executable's location.

Build this book with \api{make -C book}. Its PDF is written under
\api{book/build}. The generated toolkit chapters can be refreshed with
\api{make -C book export}. The remaining chapters are authored directly in
LaTeX, and their complete MuLL examples participate in CTest.
